INT. BOXING GYM - FORMER CHURCH SANCTUARY - EARLY MORNING

Stained glass above the ring. Pews stacked against the wall. A speed bag thuds in a corner.

BERNARD OYELOWE-STEIN (60s, trainer, towel over shoulder) holds the pads. LUZ MERCADO (20s, boxer, hand wraps frayed) slams a combination into them. Left. Right. Left.

KOFI ASARE (20s, sparring partner, headgear) waits on the ropes, bouncing slowly.

Bernard says nothing. Luz throws again. Harder.

Bernard lowers the pads.

BERNARD
Again.

She throws. He tilts his head, listening to the snap.

BERNARD (CONT'D)
Again.

Luz exhales through her nose. Throws. Her shoulder is rigid. Bernard watches her elbow.

Kofi climbs through the ropes. Offers his gloves. Luz doesn't look at him.

BERNARD (CONT'D)
Three rounds.

Luz tapes a wrist. Kofi taps his headgear twice. A bell rings somewhere above. Light through the glass lays red and blue across the canvas.

They circle.
